Template: homelab-database/listen_addresses
Type: string
Default: localhost
Description: PostgreSQL listen_addresses:
 Comma-separated list, or '*'. Leave as localhost unless other hosts
 need to reach this database over the network.

Template: homelab-database/allowed_networks
Type: string
Default:
Description: CIDR ranges to permit in pg_hba.conf (space-separated):
 e.g. "10.20.0.115/32". Leave blank for localhost-only. Each is added as
 an additive scram-sha-256 rule for "all" databases/users -- tighten by
 hand afterward in /etc/postgresql/<ver>/main/pg_hba.conf.d/90-homelab-database.conf
 if a narrower rule is wanted.

Template: homelab-database/adopt_existing
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: An existing PostgreSQL cluster was detected -- adopt it in place?
 Skip any tuning that would override values already present in
 postgresql.conf; only add new, additive settings via our own drop-in
 file. Decline to treat this as a from-scratch install instead.

Template: homelab-database/enable_backups
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Enable a basic pg_dump-based nightly backup?
 No backup mechanism exists by default. This installs a cron job dumping
 every database to /var/backups/homelab-database/, retaining 7 days.
 Decline to leave backups out of scope (e.g. if handled by external
 tooling already).
